This gives your `WebGLTileLayer` a public `setStyle()` method.  Call it with any valid style object — for example:

```js
tileLayer.setStyle({
  color: ['interpolate', ['linear'], ['band', 1], 0, 'blue', 255, 'red'],
  brightness: 0.1,
  variables: { threshold: 100 }
});
```

This will update the style in place, discard the old shaders/uniforms on the next render pass, re‐parse the new style into GLSL (via the existing `parseStyle()`), and redraw the layer without throwing away already‐fetched tiles.
